<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Catalan Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1302">1302</a>–<a href="/years/1388">1388</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Grand Catalan Company, Almogavars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Catalan Company was a band of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>, mostly Catalan and Aragonese almogavars, led first by Roger de Flor and hired by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> in 1303 against the Turks. After quarrelling with Byzantium it ravaged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> and Macedonia, then defeated and killed Duke Walter of Brienne at Halmyros in 1311 and ruled the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> until 1388.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catalan-company.jpg" alt="Catalan Company" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ramon Muntaner. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cr%C3%B2nica_de_Ramon_Muntaner.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
